WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:19.005
"Are you sure your sock is gone?" Henry asked.

2
00:00:19.006 --> 00:00:22.229
"Maybe it fell into the bottom of your bag."

3
00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.233
Maggie dumped her bag out on the bench.

4
00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:31.400
"No, it's not here. Someone stole it! Just like all my other stuff!"

5
00:00:31.401 --> 00:00:36.473
"Why would someone steal one sock?" Cole wondered.

6
00:00:36.474 --> 00:00:42.220
Maggie didn't answer. She was already stomping down the aisle of the barn.

7
00:00:42.221 --> 00:00:47.405
"Uh-oh," Henry said. "We'd better follow her."

8
00:00:47.406 --> 00:00:50.616
He knew that his cousin had a quick temper.

9
00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:57.518
If she started yelling about her sock, she might accidentally warn the thief that the boys were investigating.

10
00:00:57.519 --> 00:01:00.492
Maggie stopped in front of a horse stall.

11
00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.937
Daisy was standing in the doorway holding a saddle.

12
00:01:03.938 --> 00:01:09.426
"My sock is missing!" Maggie said. "Did you take it?"

13
00:01:09.427 --> 00:01:14.722
Daisy gave her a surprised look. "Why would I take your sock?

14
00:01:14.723 --> 00:01:18.850
I have my own." She pointed to her feet.

15
00:01:18.851 --> 00:01:22.713
Two pink socks were sticking out above her boots.

16
00:01:22.714 --> 00:01:27.166
Henry grabbed Maggie's arm as Daisy went into her horse's stall.

17
00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:33.200
"Wait," he said. "Yelling at people won't get your sock back."

18
00:01:33.201 --> 00:01:38.723
"Or any of the other stuff," added Cole. "Let us investigate."

19
00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:44.958
For a second Henry didn't think Maggie would agree. But finally she nodded.

20
00:01:44.959 --> 00:01:51.321
"Okay," she said. "But how am I supposed to ride with only one sock?"

21
00:01:51.322 --> 00:01:56.781
Cole kicked off his sneakers. "You can borrow one of mine," he said.

22
00:01:56.782 --> 00:02:02.626
"Yuck. Boys' socks stink." Maggie made a face.

23
00:02:02.627 --> 00:02:05.459
But she took the sock Cole handed her.

24
00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:09.526
"I guess I'll have to suffer if I want to ride."

25
00:02:09.527 --> 00:02:13.288
Then she stomped back toward Big Spot's stall.

26
00:02:13.289 --> 00:02:17.228
Cole took off his other sock and stuck it in his pocket.

27
00:02:17.229 --> 00:02:19.592
Then he put his shoes back on.

28
00:02:19.593 --> 00:02:24.587
"Are we really going to investigate a missing sock?" he asked Henry.

29
00:02:24.588 --> 00:02:28.060
"She probably just left it in the car or something."

30
00:02:28.061 --> 00:02:31.155
"You could be right," Henry admitted.

31
00:02:31.156 --> 00:02:36.146
"Did you notice if she had both socks in her bag when we came in?"

32
00:02:36.147 --> 00:02:39.073
Cole laughed.

33
00:02:39.074 --> 00:02:45.913
"No. I don't usually go around counting people's socks, especially when they're not even on their feet."

34
00:02:45.914 --> 00:02:51.419
That gave Henry an idea. "I know what we can do," he said.

35
00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.292
"Let's go see what socks everybody else is wearing.

36
00:02:55.293 --> 00:03:00.239
For example, we know Daisy isn't wearing Maggie's missing sock.

37
00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.887
Her socks are pink, and Maggie's are white."

38
00:03:03.888 --> 00:03:07.461
"Do you really think someone took that sock?"

39
00:03:07.462 --> 00:03:10.439
"Who knows?" Henry shrugged.

40
00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:16.448
"Maybe someone forgot a sock and decided to borrow Maggie's since she wasn't watching it."

41
00:03:16.449 --> 00:03:23.717
"Even if someone did borrow a sock, that doesn't mean that person is the barn thief," Cole said.

42
00:03:23.718 --> 00:03:26.431
"True," Henry agreed.

43
00:03:26.432 --> 00:03:31.871
"But we can watch for other suspicious behavior while we check everyone's socks."

44
00:03:31.872 --> 00:03:37.821
They walked back to Zach. By now he was putting a saddle on his pony.

45
00:03:37.822 --> 00:03:42.195
"What do you want?" he asked when he saw Henry and Cole.

46
00:03:42.196 --> 00:03:44.960
He sounded kind of grumpy.

47
00:03:44.961 --> 00:03:48.964
"Nothing." Henry looked at Zach's feet.

48
00:03:48.965 --> 00:03:52.452
He was wearing athletic socks with stripes on them.

49
00:03:52.453 --> 00:03:54.891
"Do you know where Eleanor is?"

50
00:03:54.892 --> 00:03:58.976
"Nope." Zach adjusted the pony's saddle.

51
00:03:58.977 --> 00:04:04.529
Henry and Cole walked away. "Wrong socks," Cole whispered.

52
00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:09.254
Henry nodded. "Two suspects down, one to go."

53
00:04:09.255 --> 00:04:14.938
"Only one?" Cole said. "What about Jill and Ms. Wood?"

54
00:04:14.939 --> 00:04:21.610
Henry thought about that. "I don't think Ms. Wood is a good suspect," he said.

55
00:04:21.611 --> 00:04:25.173
"Why would an adult steal a kid's stuff?

56
00:04:25.174 --> 00:04:29.569
Plus she was going to get the check from Maggie anyway.

57
00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:32.754
But we probably should investigate Jill."

58
00:04:32.755 --> 00:04:40.188
They wandered around until they found Eleanor.

59
00:04:40.189 --> 00:04:43.632
She was leading a pony out of its stall.

60
00:04:43.633 --> 00:04:49.339
Henry looked at her feet. She was wearing short boots, just like the others.

61
00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:54.094
But her pants completely covered her socks. Now what?

62
00:04:54.095 --> 00:04:59.074
Cole had an idea. "Hey, Eleanor," he said.

63
00:04:59.075 --> 00:05:02.346
"Is that a bug crawling up your pant leg?"

64
00:05:02.347 --> 00:05:07.635
"What? Which leg?" Eleanor shrieked.

65
00:05:07.636 --> 00:05:11.780
She dropped the pony's reins and yanked up both pant legs.

66
00:05:11.781 --> 00:05:14.617
Her socks were brown.

67
00:05:14.618 --> 00:05:18.258
"Sorry, I guess I was wrong," Cole said.

68
00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:21.125
Eleanor gave him an angry look.

69
00:05:21.126 --> 00:05:26.830
Then she grabbed her pony's reins and hurried off.

70
00:05:26.831 --> 00:05:30.133
"Good trick," Henry said with a grin.

71
00:05:30.134 --> 00:05:34.050
"I guess it proved that nobody is wearing that sock.

72
00:05:34.051 --> 00:05:37.564
Maybe Maggie did leave it in the car."

73
00:05:37.565 --> 00:05:42.137
"Or maybe Big Spot grabbed it," Cole suggested.

74
00:05:42.138 --> 00:05:45.269
"Maggie left her bag sitting right by his stall."

75
00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:50.404
"Yeah. Let's go check."

76
00:05:50.405 --> 00:05:57.536
They hurried back to Big Spot's stall. The pony was gone. So was Maggie.

77
00:05:57.537 --> 00:06:01.916
"I guess the riding lesson started," Henry said.

78
00:06:01.917 --> 00:06:06.901
Cole looked into the pony's stall. "I don't see the sock in here.

79
00:06:06.902 --> 00:06:11.929
Maybe Spot ate it. He wanted to eat Maggie's hair, remember?"

80
00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.970
Henry shrugged.

81
00:06:13.971 --> 00:06:21.800
"Maybe. But he definitely didn't eat that brush that disappeared or Maggie's charm bracelet.

82
00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:25.741
We have to find that thief!"
